Hmm.  The "it" in this case is a length of time
- a sun's "useful life", a concept I've tried to
convey with {selxaktei}.  A typical sun whose outer
layers of hydrogen have been stripped off should be
able to support life on its attendant planet(s)
longer than a typical sun whose outer layers of
hydrogen have not been stripped off.  The more
massive the sun, the shorter its span of usefulness.
Removing the outer layers of hydrogen would reduce
the sun's mass & should prolong its "useful life".
